{"id": "xpakistan", "name": "Deosai National Park", "short": "Deosai", "place": "Pakistan", "lat": 35.0, "lon": 75.4, "side": "r", "cont": "Asia", "country": "Pakistan", "blurb": "High plateau of sedge meadows, marmots and a small brown bear population.", "tip": {"id": "marmot", "title": "Remove the marmots", "text": "Marmots are prey for wolves, snow leopards, eagles and bears. Set Himalayan marmot to -100% and watch those predators and the vulture that scavenges."}, "kind": "Polar & mountain", "park": true, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Deosai National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deosai_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Himalayan brown bear", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Himalayan_brown_bear"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Himalayan marmot", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Himalayan_marmot"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Siberian ibex", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siberian_ibex"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Himalayan wolf", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Himalayan_wolf"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Bearded vulture", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bearded_vulture"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Deosai National Park", "icon": "grizzly", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "summer sunlight", "xh": 0.12, "desc": "The plateau is reachable only in the short summer, and that brief warm season is when its plants grow and flower."}, {"id": "melt", "sp": "snowmelt and marsh", "xh": 0.4}, {"id": "snow", "sp": "winter snow cover", "xh": 0.68, "desc": "Heavy winter snow closes the plateau for much of the year. Bears and marmots sleep through it in dens and burrows."}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.9, "name": "Soil microbes and fungi", "desc": "Break down dead sedges, dung and carcasses on the cold plateau and return nutrients to the thin soil."}, {"id": "carex", "sp": "carex deasyi", "xh": 0.1}, {"id": "festuca", "sp": "festuca kashmiriana", "xh": 0.32}, {"id": "astragalus", "sp": "astragalus rhizanthus", "xh": 0.54}, {"id": "saussurea", "sp": "saussurea falconeri", "xh": 0.76}, {"id": "marmot", "sp": "marmota himalayana", "xh": 0.08, "desc": "A colonial burrower of alpine grassland that eats grasses and flowering herbs and hibernates for about seven months. Prey for many predators."}, {"id": "ibex", "sp": "capra sibirica", "xh": 0.2, "desc": "A mountain goat of rocky slopes that eats mainly grasses and sedges in summer. Wolves, snow leopards and brown bears hunt it."}, {"id": "vole", "sp": "hyperacrius fertilis", "xh": 0.32}, {"id": "snowcock", "sp": "tetraogallus himalayensis", "xh": 0.44, "desc": "A large mountain gamebird listed among the birds of the plateau. It feeds on plants of the high slopes."}, {"id": "lark", "sp": "eremophila alpestris", "xh": 0.56, "name": "Horned lark", "tl": 2, "wiki": "Horned lark"}, {"id": "colias", "sp": "colias fieldii", "xh": 0.68}, {"id": "bear", "sp": "ursus arctos", "xh": 0.14, "name": "Himalayan brown bear", "tl": 3, "wiki": "Himalayan brown bear", "desc": "A critically endangered omnivore that eats grasses, roots, berries, insects and small mammals. Deosai holds its most stable population."}, {"id": "stoat", "sp": "mustela erminea", "xh": 0.34, "desc": "A small weasel that hunts rodents and ground birds; GloBI records it eating horned larks.", "ic": "fox"}, {"id": "kestrel", "sp": "falco tinnunculus", "xh": 0.54, "desc": "A small falcon that hovers over open ground to take rodents and small birds; GloBI records it eating horned larks."}, {"id": "vulture", "sp": "gypaetus barbatus", "xh": 0.74, "desc": "A scavenger that lives mostly on bone and carrion from hoofed animals, and sometimes takes small live prey such as marmots."}, {"id": "wolf", "sp": "canis lupus", "xh": 0.2, "na